---
// The motivation section, three beats. Static copy; the wording is owner-approved verbatim.
---

<section class="section why-relab" aria-labelledby="why-relab-heading">
  <h2 id="why-relab-heading">Why R9lab exists</h2>
  <div class="why-beats">
    <div class="why-beat">
      <h3 class="why-beat-label">Closed, and too slow</h3>
      <p>
        Circular-economy research depends on detailed product data: what things are made of, how
        they come apart, which parts matter. That data is scarce, mostly closed, and slow to
        produce. Producers hold it as proprietary, and small expert teams sampling by hand cannot
        keep pace with what reaches the market.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="why-beat">
      <h3 class="why-beat-label">Downstream, at the point of failure</h3>
      <p>
        So R9lab goes downstream, to the people who already open products: repairers, refurbishers,
        dismantlers, recyclers. They meet products at the point of failure, a vantage that
        captures as-failed composition, wear, and recoverability that as-designed specifications
        never show.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="why-beat">
      <h3 class="why-beat-label">What contributors get back</h3>
      {/* Keep the return of value in the future tense: paper 1 says it is not
          built and the pilot did not test it. Never imply R9lab performs
          R-strategy analysis. */}
      <p>
        Records feed the data that circular-economy research and product design rely on.
        Contributors will get something back as well: composition insight and sustainability metrics
        for the products they open. That part is coming in a later release.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .why-relab h2 {
    margin: 0 0 1.4rem;
  }

  .why-beats {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 2rem;
  }

  /* Hairline top rule per beat: a flat drafting divider, no shadow. */
  .why-beat {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-page-border);
    padding-top: 0.9rem;
  }

  /* The subhead role, like every other h3: these are phrases, not measurements,
     so they stay out of mono. */
  .why-beat-label {
    margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
    font-size: var(--r9lab-type-heading-size);
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: var(--r9lab-type-heading-line);
  }

  .why-beat p {
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 60ch;
    font-size: var(--font-size-body-compact);
    line-height: var(--line-height-body-compact);
  }

  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .why-beats {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 1.4rem;
    }
  }
</style>
